’Reilly had won the 500 and 1000 m, Kim had won the 1500 m and Lee the 3000 m."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The favourites all survived until the semi-finals. In the first heat, O’Reilly fell and finished last, while Lee and " [:a {:href "/athletes/95329"} "Mike McMillen"] " both broke the World Record to qualify for the final. They were joined there by Kim and Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/84158"} "Frédéric Blackburn"] ". The two Koreans decided to make it a fast race, and went all out from the start. Blackburn and McMillen managed to cling on. Kim finished the race unchallenged in another World Record, while Blackburn passed Lee just in time for the silver medal. Kim became South Korea’s first ever Winter Olympic Champion, two days after the nation had gained its first ever Winter Olympic medal in speed skating."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Helmet Nr"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Best Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "43"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/87949"} "Kim Gi-Hun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "11"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/84158"} "Frédéric Blackburn"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "45"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/89504"} "Lee Jun-Ho"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px;